# Upstream-Commit: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/72c729f354d71697a1402720c90b57ff521b6739
#
# "[bazel] Add support for --incompatible_disallow_empty_glob" (#85999),
# regenerated for this release the way upstream did it: every include pattern
# that matches nothing in this tree is removed, globs with no live pattern
# left are dropped together with the targets that only existed to hold them
# (MLPolicies, SDBM, OpenACCToLLVM, TestTypeDialect, quantops_tests,
# scf_tests), and `allow_empty = True` is set only where upstream set it: the
# per-target globs in llvm/BUILD.bazel and the clang-tidy macro, which are
# legitimately empty for some targets. The set of dead patterns is this
# release's rather than upstream's, so the hunks differ from the commit, but
# the mechanism is the same and the shipped .bazelrc enables the flag like
# upstream's does.
diff --git a/.bazelrc b/.bazelrc
index 5271cd16a..742181d4e 100644
--- a/.bazelrc
+++ b/.bazelrc
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@ build --features=layering_check
 # See: https://bazel.build/reference/be/functions#exports_files
 build --incompatible_no_implicit_file_export
 
+# Enable so downstream users can flip this flag globally, this should
+# eventually become the default
+common --incompatible_disallow_empty_glob
+
 ###############################################################################
 # Options to select different strategies for linking potential dependent
 # libraries. The default leaves it disabled.
